{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>תָּמִים תִּהְיֶה עִם ה׳</b> — meaning: since He commanded him just before not to divine or practice sorcery and not to inquire of a ghost, etc., He said <b>תָּמִים</b> etc. — meaning to say, the reason for all these things is to know the future and to conduct oneself according to what they instruct and to remedy the deficiency as one is able to do. If you are with HaShem, you shall be תָּמִים — nothing will be lacking for you, and whatever the constellation declares concerning you will not come true for harm. And this is your sign: Abraham, who walked before HaShem — even though the constellation showed concerning him that he would not beget children, it was reversed and he begot (Shabbat 156a). And accordingly, the word <b>תִּהְיֶה</b> extends upward and downward in this manner: 'תָּמִים you shall be if you are with HaShem,' or in this manner: 'תָּמִים you shall be when you are with your El.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:58.956073816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}